
Changes with AppServe 0.3.0                                      07 Oct 2026

    *) Change: application request handling uses one thread per worker
       process; threads and thread_stack_size configuration and Ruby thread
       hooks are removed.

    *) Change: libunit and Go request handling are simplified to use one
       thread; worker process state is separated from ports.

    *) Feature: configuration API responses include application startup
       error details.

    *) Feature: status reports worker pool max, spare, busy, and idle
       counts; connection statistics and running and starting worker fields
       are removed.

    *) Feature: application and global status report total, active, queued,
       completed, and failed requests, response status classes, and request
       latency in milliseconds.

    *) Feature: request latency statistics include approximate cumulative
       P95 and P99 percentiles; global percentiles use merged application
       latency samples.

    *) Feature: application and global process statistics count abnormal
       worker exits; normal recycling and prototype exits are excluded.

    *) Bugfix: thread startup, configuration mapping alignment, MurmurHash2
       shifts, and empty-string formatting are corrected.

    *) Change: README documentation describes features and quick start; the
       migration guide and packaging references are removed.


Changes with AppServe 0.2.0                                      05 Oct 2026

    *) Change: Java, Node.js, and Perl application support and related
       packages and container images are removed.

    *) Change: listeners pass requests directly to fixed applications and
       targets; built-in routing, configuration variables, and NJS
       expressions are removed.

    *) Change: built-in TLS, static file serving, reverse proxying, upstream
       load balancing, and access logging are removed.

    *) Change: certificate and JavaScript module control APIs and the
       OpenSSL, PCRE, and NJS dependencies are removed.

    *) Feature: standard Forwarded header processing with listener
       forwarded.trusted IP/CIDR rules replaces legacy client_ip and
       X-Forwarded-* configuration.

    *) Change: unused job, cache, buffer filter, buffer pool, fiber, memory
       zone, vector, time parsing, and sendfile code is removed.


Changes with AppServe 0.1.0                                      05 Oct 2026

    *) Feature: initial AppServe release with runtime configuration and
       multi-language application hosting.

    *) Change: daemon, packages, services, default paths, and server
       identification use AppServe names; application API and binding
       identifiers are retained.
